    <md:title>3.1.2: Self Check</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e5285097-9f49-48b2-92d8-16b830f0d9b6</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para dir="ltr">The plot below is a scatter plot of mean temperature in July and mean inches of rain per year for a sample of midwestern cities. A line is drawn to fit the data. </para>
<para dir="ltr"><figure><media alt="A SCATTER PLOT THAT SHOWS MEAN TEMPERATURE IN JULY IN DEGREES FAHRENHEIT ON THE X-AXIS AND MEAN RAINFALL PER YEAR IN INCHES ON THE Y-AXIS. THE LINE DRAWN INCREASES FROM LEFT TO RIGHT."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/afb399190f61185c419bb2d99e3317cec9ab4976"/></media></figure></para>
<para dir="ltr">Use the line provided to predict the mean number of inches of rain per year for a city that has a mean temperature of 70°F in July. </para></section>
</content>
